        "original_id": "422be332-33ed-558b-a537-386f838f52fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1974 South African Grand Prix\n- Places: Kyalami, Midrand, Gauteng, South Africa\n- Products: BRM P201\n- People: Jean-Pierre Beltoise\n- Topics: Formula One, motor racing\n\nFacts:\n- The 1974 South African Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held at Kyalami on 30 March 1974.\n- Kyalami Racing Circuit is a motor racing circuit in Midrand, Gauteng, South Africa.\n- The name Kyalami comes from the Zulu phrase \"Khaya lami,\" meaning \"My home.\"\n- Jean-Pierre Beltoise finished second in the BRM P201 at the 1974 South African Grand Prix.\n- The BRM P201 achieved its best finish with second place on its debut at the 1974 South African Grand Prix.",
